xnu 0285: the refresh CoreAnimation paces its display link on

The framebuffer published its mode list (TimingElements, 16.16 fixed point) and
nothing else, so the window server's display link had no interval to be paced
against. IOMFBDisplayRefresh is the property CoreAnimation reads: its minimum,
maximum and step are 32.32 fixed point (seconds times 2^32), and only
displayRefreshStepMachTime is in Mach absolute ticks. HakiOS measured the wrong
unit on its own port: with ticks in all four fields CoreAnimation took the panel
for a 26844 Hz one and paced every frame against that.

The rate is MONDRIAN_FB_REFRESH_HZ, the same 60 the timing elements and the
vsync timer already use, so the three descriptions of the display cannot drift
apart.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -253,6 +253,42 @@
 	OSSafeReleaseNULL(color);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The refresh CoreAnimation runs its display link on.
+ *
+ * IOMFBDisplayRefresh carries the interval three times and the step once:
+ * displayMinRefreshInterval, displayMaxRefreshInterval and displayRefreshStep
+ * are 32.32 fixed point (seconds times 2^32), and only
+ * displayRefreshStepMachTime is in Mach absolute ticks. HakiOS measured what
+ * the wrong unit does: with ticks in all four fields CoreAnimation took the
+ * panel for a 26844 Hz one and paced every frame against that (0dedaec6).
+ * The timing elements above say the same rate in 16.16, which is what the
+ * mode list wants; this is the property the window server's display link
+ * reads.
+ */
+static void
+mondrian_publish_refresh(IOService *fb, uint32_t hz)
+{
+	OSDictionary *refresh;
+	uint64_t interval, ticks = 0;
+
+	if (hz == 0) {
+		return;
+	}
+	refresh = OSDictionary::withCapacity(4);
+	if (refresh == NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
+	interval = (1ULL << 32) / hz;
+	nanoseconds_to_absolutetime(1000000000ULL / hz, &ticks);
+	mondrian_set_number(refresh, "displayMinRefreshInterval", interval);
+	mondrian_set_number(refresh, "displayMaxRefreshInterval", interval);
+	mondrian_set_number(refresh, "displayRefreshStep", interval);
+	mondrian_set_number(refresh, "displayRefreshStepMachTime", ticks);
+	fb->setProperty("IOMFBDisplayRefresh", refresh);
+	refresh->release();
+}
+
 class IOMobileFramebufferUserClient;
 
 /* Four pixels of the canvas, stored as one 16-byte write. */
